<title>CHINA: China drops import licence, quotas on rolled steel.</title>
<headline>China drops import licence, quotas on rolled steel.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>China is to scrap import licences and quotas for rolled steel, the People's Daily Overseas Edition said on Monday.</p>
<p>In past years, all imports were made under a planned system requiring licences and quotas, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>The move by the Ministry of Foreign Trade and Economic Cooperation, the State Planning Commission, the State Economic and Trade Commission and the General Administration of Customs could ensure an appropriate use of steel while preventing excessive imports, it said.</p>
<p>-- Beijing newsroom, (8610) 6532 1921</p>
